## Step 4: two defects the installed toolchain exposed

Both defects pre-date this track; the guard folder had no `node_modules`, so
no command of the plugin could run before Task 1.2.

1. `plugins/opencode-measure-guard/tests/allow-adversarial.test.ts` case V18
   expected a CR-only allow entry to load as a folder. The parser rejects
   every entry with a C0 control character since commit 6d2fdcf, and
   `mods/measure-guard/README.md` states that rule (row 1). The sibling
   cases V6 and V7 were updated in that commit; V18 was left behind and
   failed. V18 now expects the folder list to be empty and the ignore reason
   to be `has a control character`. The case still proves that no real path
   opens.
2. `src/core/guards.ts` returned `match[1]` under `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`,
   so `bun x tsc --noEmit -p .` failed with TS2322. The fix is
   `match[1] ?? null`; the regex always fills the group, so the runtime
   behaviour does not change. The shared core lives in three copies, and the
   two parity gates require identical copies, so the same one line changed
   `mods/measure-guard/hooks/guards.ts` and
   `plugins/dsh-measure-guard/src/core/guards.ts` as well. Those two folders
   sit outside the scope of the spec.

